      {
        "display": "A box plot has Q1 = 20 and Q3 = 44. An outlier is defined as more than \\(1.5 \\times \\text{IQR}\\) beyond the quartiles. Find the lower outlier boundary.",
        "solutions": [
          -16
        ],
        "calculator": false,
        "input_type": "single_value",
        "misconceptions": [
          {
            "check": "common",
            "expect": 56,
            "message": "IQR = 24. 1.5 × 24 = 36. Lower fence = Q1 − 36 = 20 − 36 = −16.",
            "pattern": "wrong_formula",
            "expect_note": "Student adds instead of subtracts: Q1 + 1.5 × IQR = 20 + 36 = 56, computing the upper outlier fence instead of the lower."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "display": "A histogram and a CF curve both represent the same data. The histogram bar 20-30 has fd = 4.5. Total data = 120. What percentage of data falls in this class?",
